{"id":"92e9c5c40b78fb74","group":"72","path":"72/72-thm-identity-free-bounded-soundness.md","title":"thm identity free bounded soundness","display":"thm identity free bounded soundness","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Handbook of Proof Theory","book_abbrev":"72","label":"72-thm-identity-free-bounded-soundness","aliases":["72-thm-identity-free-bounded-soundness"],"display":"thm identity free bounded soundness","depends_on":["[[72-df-identity-free-program-calculus]]","[[72-df-finite-envelope-iteration]]","[[72-thm-least-adequate-lower-structure]]"],"source_edition":"Buss (ed.), Handbook of Proof Theory, Elsevier, 1998","source_location":"Ch.IX Theorem4.2.4, print658/PDF670; assignment and finite-set formulation","verification_status":"source-statement-checked; local rule induction checked","proof_status":"proved-in-note by induction on the displayed finite-height derivability","eligible_as_verified_dependency":false},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Handbook of Proof Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"72"},{"key":"label","html":"72-thm-identity-free-bounded-soundness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>72-thm-identity-free-bounded-soundness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm identity free bounded soundness"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"62a32ca4e63fca90\" href=\"?note=62a32ca4e63fca90\" title=\"72-df-identity-free-program-calculus\">72-df-identity-free-program-calculus</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"7fdc7a7a93d79109\" href=\"?note=7fdc7a7a93d79109\" title=\"72-df-finite-envelope-iteration\">72-df-finite-envelope-iteration</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"aeeeb6862efb50c6\" href=\"?note=aeeeb6862efb50c6\" title=\"72-thm-least-adequate-lower-structure\">72-thm-least-adequate-lower-structure</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"Buss (ed.), Handbook of Proof Theory, Elsevier, 1998"},{"key":"source_location","html":"Ch.IX Theorem4.2.4, print658/PDF670; assignment and finite-set formulation"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked; local rule induction checked"},{"key":"proof_status","html":"proved-in-note by induction on the displayed finite-height derivability"},{"key":"eligible_as_verified_dependency","html":"false"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\\vdash_r^{-n}\\Gamma\">\\(P\\vdash_r^{-n}\\Gamma\\)</span> 采用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"62a32ca4e63fca90\" href=\"?note=62a32ca4e63fca90\" title=\"72-df-identity-free-program-calculus\">72-df-identity-free-program-calculus</a> 的有限集合推导；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M_P^{[n]}\">\\(M_P^{[n]}\\)</span> 采用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"7fdc7a7a93d79109\" href=\"?note=7fdc7a7a93d79109\" title=\"72-df-finite-envelope-iteration\">72-df-finite-envelope-iteration</a>。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> 是固定基底 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D\">\\(D\\)</span> 上的四值结构，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Lower}(M)\">\\(\\operatorname{Lower}(M)\\)</span> 采用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"aeeeb6862efb50c6\" href=\"?note=aeeeb6862efb50c6\" title=\"72-thm-least-adequate-lower-structure\">72-thm-least-adequate-lower-structure</a>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{EqBase}_\\Sigma(M)\">\\(\\operatorname{EqBase}_\\Sigma(M)\\)</span> 采用 calculus 的 CET 上游。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V=\\mathrm{Var}_S\">\\(V=\\mathrm{Var}_S\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"s\">\\(s\\)</span> 遍历 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D^V\">\\(D^V\\)</span>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n,r\\in\\omega\">\\(n,r\\in\\omega\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma\\in\\mathsf{Seq}_\\Sigma\">\\(\\Gamma\\in\\mathsf{Seq}_\\Sigma\\)</span>；下式对空 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma\">\\(\\Gamma\\)</span> 也适用。前提 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\\sqsubseteq\\mathcal E_P(M)\">\\(M\\sqsubseteq\\mathcal E_P(M)\\)</span> 是初始结构的递增条件，不替换成充分性所要求的反向不等式。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{EqBase}_\\Sigma(M)\\land\\operatorname{Lower}(M)\\land M\\sqsubseteq\\mathcal E_P(M)\\land P\\vdash^{-n}_{r}\\Gamma\n\\ \\Longrightarrow\\ \\forall s\\in D^V\\ \\exists A\\in\\Gamma\\ (⟦ A⟧_{M_P^{[n]},s}=\\mathsf t).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\operatorname{EqBase}_\\Sigma(M)\\land\\operatorname{Lower}(M)\\land M\\sqsubseteq\\mathcal E_P(M)\\land P\\vdash^{-n}_{r}\\Gamma\n\\ \\Longrightarrow\\ \\forall s\\in D^V\\ \\exists A\\in\\Gamma\\ (⟦ A⟧_{M_P^{[n]},s}=\\mathsf t).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>这是 Theorem 4.2.4 在当前编码下的陈述；页图 PDF670 核对了初始不等式方向和高度/阶段同为 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>。lower 子集对公式解释及 envelope 封闭，递增条件使各阶段递增。按推导高度归纳，较低高度前提的真值可传到同一当前阶段：逻辑规则由相应布尔正坐标运算及替换引理成立；全称规则用 eigenvariable 的新鲜条件遍历赋值。CET 公理只依赖基底，所以所有阶段保真。program rule 若上下文未已为真，前提定义式在上一阶段为真，下一阶段相应字面量便由 envelope 定义为真。</p>\n<p>cut 情形若结论上下文没有真公式，两个前提会分别迫使 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> 与 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sim A\">\\(\\sim A\\)</span> 在同一 lower 阶段为真，这要求 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> 同时有两个证据坐标 1，与 lower 封闭性矛盾。初始公理处理高度 0；闭包中沿用旧阶段的分支由阶段递增性处理。此证明没有把 identity 公理加入系统；若加入，初始全 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf u\">\\(\\mathsf u\\)</span> 结构上的 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R(c),\\overline R(c)\">\\(R(c),\\overline R(c)\\)</span> 就给出反例。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Asserti